@{
    'chromium-target-absent'    = 'The Chromium scenario looks for exactly one target, Obsidian (Electron) at %LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\Obsidian\Obsidian.exe, and checks no browser or other Electron app; Edge is absent under this grounding (G5). When that file is missing every Chromium leg reports this skip with the path it checked, rather than a silent pass.'
    'foreground-grant-declined' = 'A raw SetForegroundWindow (AttachThreadInput + AllowSetForegroundWindow) staged from the long-lived harness process itself can be declined by this desktop even after every documented workaround, the same escape hatch crates/windows/src/system/signal/wait_event_live_tests.rs already takes for focus_changed ("this desktop declines foreground even to a raw SetForegroundWindow"). Declared for the contended focus-steal control (R17b(c)) so an unstageable host reports a visible skip rather than a silent pass; the N-trial rate leg is never reached when the control cannot be established.'
    'shell-surface-absent'      = 'A runner whose shell does not expose the surface a leg drives: open-system-surface answers INVALID_ARGS (the informative build refusal), or TIMEOUT on a server SKU where no ShellExperienceHost process runs to present it, instead of an identity. Declared for the Action Center legs of the shell-surfaces scenario so a surface-less host reports a visible skip, with the OS build and the shell host read beside it, rather than a silent pass or a fake failure. A TIMEOUT on a workstation SKU or with the host running stays a failure.'
    'shell-tray-toolbar-absent' = 'A shell with no promoted notification-area ToolbarWindow32 (the harness COM trayscan finds none) on which snapshot --surface system-tray answers WINDOW_NOT_FOUND: the count leg has no surface to count and no independent count to compare. Declared for the tray count leg so such a shell reports a visible skip with the trayscan flags and the OS build. If the binary opens a tray the COM read cannot find, the leg fails as a disagreement, and any other refusal fails as a failure of the binary.'
}
